WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Program · 01/04 Initial State
FG is shown with fewer electrons.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Program · 02/04 Apply Conditions
coupling and tunneling terminals establish oxide field.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.008
Program · 03/04 Carrier Motion
electrons enter FG from a MOS tunneling region by FN tunneling.

4
00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.508
Program · 04/04 Retained Result
field removal leaves increased FG charge.

5
00:00:11.508 --> 00:00:14.008
Read · 01/04 Retained State
two FG charge states create different thresholds.

6
00:00:14.008 --> 00:00:16.508
Read · 02/04 Select the Cell
selectors enable the read channel.

7
00:00:16.508 --> 00:00:20.142
Read · 03/04 Sense the Path
Path: sense channel conductance without FN charge transfer.

8
00:00:20.142 --> 00:00:22.642
Read · 04/04 Compare the Result
Result: compare against a reference while preserving FG charge.

9
00:00:22.642 --> 00:00:25.142
Erase · 01/04 Programmed State
FG retains programmed charge.

10
00:00:25.142 --> 00:00:27.642
Erase · 02/04 Switch Terminal Conditions
switch terminal conditions to establish charge-removal field.

11
00:00:27.642 --> 00:00:31.650
Erase · 03/04 Remove Electrons
electrons leave FG by FN tunneling into a MOS receiving region.

12
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.150
Erase · 04/04 Ready to Reprogram
Result: reduced FG charge permits another program cycle.

13
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.650
Read · 01/04 Retained State
two FG charge states create different thresholds.

14
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.150
Read · 02/04 Select the Cell
selectors enable the read channel.

15
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.783
Read · 03/04 Sense the Path
Path: sense channel conductance without FN charge transfer.

16
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:45.283
Read · 04/04 Compare the Result
Result: compare against a reference while preserving FG charge.
